# AllieMinate's own Google Cloud OAuth client (Desktop app type). Lets "Add Google Account" work out
# of the box for anyone who downloads a built .dmg/.exe, with no per-user Google Cloud project setup.
#
# NOT loaded at runtime and NOT read by config.ts directly — build-app.sh's pristine-bundle stage reads
# this file and injects these two lines into the DISTRIBUTED .env (the one shipped inside the app),
# separately from a developer's own personal .env (which keeps real connected accounts and never ships).
#
# This real file (apps/backend/.oauth-defaults.env, no .example suffix) is gitignored on purpose —
# GitHub's push protection rejects a plaintext OAuth client secret outright, so it never gets committed.
# To set this up yourself: copy this file to apps/backend/.oauth-defaults.env and fill in a real OAuth
# Desktop-app client from https://console.cloud.google.com (APIs & Services > Credentials).
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
